---
import SitePage from '../components/SitePage.astro';
import { links } from '../data/site';
---

<SitePage title="Extensions" description="Run Pi's TypeScript extensions and packages, or shape the harness in C#.">
	<div class="ps-pagehead">
		<h1 class="ps-h1">Pi's extensions, or yours in C#</h1>
		<p class="ps-lede">PiSharp runs Pi's TypeScript extensions and packages as they are. You can also add tools, slash commands and lifecycle hooks with a plain C# class, loaded from the same folders.</p>
	</div>

	<div class="lanes">
		<div class="ps-card">
			<h2 class="ps-h3">Pi's TypeScript extensions</h2>
			<p class="ps-muted">Drop them in <code>~/.pi/agent/extensions</code> or install a package with <code>pisharp install</code>. PiSharp runs them in Node on Pi's own npm packages, with the whole extension API.</p>
			<p><a href="/docs/extensions/node-bridge/">Run TypeScript extensions</a></p>
		</div>
		<div class="ps-card">
			<h2 class="ps-h3">Native C# extensions</h2>
			<p class="ps-muted">Implement <code>IPiSharpExtension</code>, add a <code>pisharp-extension.json</code>, and put the folder next to your Pi extensions. In-process and typed, with no Node.</p>
			<p><a href="/docs/extensions/build-an-extension/">Build a C# extension</a></p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<section class="ps-section">
		<h2 class="ps-h2">Same extension, two languages</h2>
		<p class="ps-muted intro">The TypeScript version runs in PiSharp as it is. The C# sample is a port of it. If you've written one for Pi, you already know the shape.</p>
		<div class="pair">
			<div class="ps-term">
				<div class="ps-termbar"><span>todo.ts</span><span>TypeScript, for Pi</span></div>
				<pre class="ps-termbody"><span class="k">export default function</span> (pi: <span class="t">ExtensionAPI</span>) {'{'}
  pi.<span class="t">registerTool</span>({'{'}
    name: "todo",
    label: "Todo",
    description: "Manage a todo list. …",
    parameters: TodoParams,

    <span class="k">async</span> execute(_id, params, …) {'{'}
      <span class="k">switch</span> (params.action) {'{'} <span class="c">/* … */</span> {'}'}
    {'}'},
  {'}'});
{'}'}</pre>
			</div>
			<div class="ps-term">
				<div class="ps-termbar"><span>StatefulTodoExtension.cs</span><span>C#, for PiSharp</span></div>
				<pre class="ps-termbody"><span class="k">public sealed class</span> <span class="t">StatefulTodoExtension</span>
    : <span class="t">IPiSharpExtension</span>
{'{'}
  <span class="k">public</span> ValueTask InitializeAsync(
      IExtensionRegistry registry, CancellationToken ct)
  {'{'}
    registry.<span class="t">RegisterTool</span>(<span class="k">new</span>("todo", "todo",
        Description, JsonData.Parse(ParametersJson),
        ExecuteAsync));
    <span class="k">return</span> ValueTask.CompletedTask;
  {'}'}
{'}'}</pre>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="ps-section">
		<h2 class="ps-h2">Samples</h2>
		<ul class="ps-rows samples">
			<li>
				<strong><a class="ps-mono" href={`${links.samples}/StatefulTodo`}>StatefulTodo</a></strong>
				<span>A todo tool whose state is rebuilt from the current session branch, so it stays correct when you branch. A tool, ported from Pi.</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a class="ps-mono" href={`${links.samples}/SessionCheckpoint`}>SessionCheckpoint</a></strong>
				<span>Registers a <code>/checkpoint</code> command, a session-start observer and a pre-switch handler that saves and restores session checkpoints. Commands and session hooks.</span>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="ps-section">
		<h2 class="ps-h2">Community extensions</h2>
		<p class="ps-muted intro">Pi packages install with <code>pisharp install</code>. A catalog of C# extensions will appear here. Building one? Open an issue on <a href={links.issues}>GitHub</a> so it can be listed.</p>
	</section>
</SitePage>

<style>
	.lanes {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(20rem, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-bottom: 5.5rem;
	}
	.lanes p {
		font-size: 0.9688rem;
	}
	.intro {
		max-width: 44rem;
	}
	.pair {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(22rem, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}
	.samples {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		max-width: 48rem;
	}
	.samples li:last-child {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
	}
	.samples a {
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.samples a:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
	@media (max-width: 26rem) {
		.lanes,
		.pair {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
